    "technical_description": "llama.cpp is a plain C/C++ library and set of command-line tools that performs LLM inference with minimal dependencies across a wide range of hardware, including CPUs, Apple Silicon, NVIDIA/AMD GPUs, and accelerators via backends like Metal, CUDA, HIP, Vulkan, and SYCL. It uses the GGUF model format with integer quantization and offers a lightweight OpenAI-compatible HTTP server (llama-server) plus a CLI for chat, completion, perplexity measurement, and benchmarking.",
